From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 00:10:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] d3d12: Keep other queues' timestamp values in a ring-less
 queue's resolves.

A queue resolving timestamps that another queue sampled (behind a
fence) has no counter ring of its own, since its calls sample nothing.
Its resolves read the query heap's own counter buffer, which nobody
sampled into, and wrote zeros.

Resolves fall back to the heap's counter buffer only when this queue's
ring could not be created; otherwise they copy the values the sampling
queue wrote.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/d3d12/d3d12_command_queue.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/d3d12/d3d12_command_queue.cpp b/src/d3d12/d3d12_command_queue.cpp
index 738a13a..61f0aa5 100644
--- a/src/d3d12/d3d12_command_queue.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d12/d3d12_command_queue.cpp
@@ -1421,7 +1421,10 @@ public:
         auto from = scope.inflight.resolves.insert(
             scope.inflight.resolves.end(), pCommandList->timestamp_resolves.begin(), pCommandList->timestamp_resolves.end()
         );
-        if (!sampling_) // Task F4: sampled into the heaps' own counter buffers
+        // Task F4: this queue sampled into the heaps' own counter buffers. A queue that never sampled (no ring) keeps
+        // the values: another queue's ring wrote them. ponytail: a heap sampled by a queue whose ring failed, resolved
+        // on one with a ring, reads the values array (zeros); per-heap buffers go with Ruling 27's follow-up.
+        if (ring_failed_)
           for (; from != scope.inflight.resolves.end(); ++from)
             from->values = nullptr;
       }
